# Early Returns Required

- Applies to `.cs` source changes.
- Prefer early returns to reduce nesting and keep the main execution path clear.
- Handle guard conditions first and return immediately when prerequisites are not met.
- Avoid `else` blocks when the `if` branch already exits via `return`, `continue`, or `break`.
- Keep methods flat and readable by using explicit guard clauses for invalid or edge-case input.

## Examples

```text
Instead of:
if (condition)
{
    // main logic
}

Prefer:
if (!condition)
{
    return;
}

// main logic
```
